        "file": "docs/kill-chain.md",
        "code": "# Kill Chain educacional\n\nAdaptado do modelo Lockheed Martin Cyber Kill Chain — para slides.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[Recon] --> B[Weaponize]\n    B --> C[Deliver]\n    C --> D[Exploit]\n    D --> E[Install]\n    E --> F[C2]\n    F --> G[Actions]\n```\n\n## Mapeamento DangerZone\n\n| Fase | O que o lab ilustra | Defesa (labs 06–09) |\n|------|---------------------|---------------------|\n| Deliver | Vetor / seed | IOC de entrada |\n| Exploit/Install | Marcador no VFS | Hash integrity |\n| C2 / Exfil | Eventos `exfil` | Detector + score |\n| Actions | Encrypt / keylog | YARA-like + alerts |\n\n## Contenção rápida (talking points)\n\n1. Isolar host seed (worm)\n2. Restaurar de backup imutável (ransomware)\n3. Rotacionar credenciais (trojan/spyware)\n4. Baseline de hashes + EDR (vírus)",
